Step 1 -- which operators are selection rules?
Family (1) scan for '*':
  Every '*' output has 4 symbol(s), so a selection must pick exactly 4 position(s).
  From e1 (](*/| = ](/|): A0=] A1=( B0=/ B1=|.
  Output symbol 1 is ( -> copied from A1.
  Output symbol 2 of e1 is ], which is none of A0,A1,B0,B1 -> no selection can produce it -> no selection rule.
Family (1) scan for '-':
  e2's output has 2 symbols but e3's has 3; one fixed selection always copies the same number of positions -> no selection rule.
So family (2) must explain operator(s) '*', '-': one shared digit cipher covering all their examples plus the query symbols.
